      "text": "To determine the volume of the sphere inscribed within a cube, we first need to recognize that the sphere is tangent to all the faces of the cube. This means the diameter of the sphere is equal to the edge length of the cube.\n\nGiven the cube's edge length is 6 inches, the diameter of the sphere is also 6 inches. Therefore, the radius \\( r \\) of the sphere is half of the diameter:\n\\[\nr = \\frac{6}{2} = 3 \\text{ inches}\n\\]\n\nThe formula for the volume \\( V \\) of a sphere is:\n\\[\nV = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi r^3\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the radius \\( r = 3 \\) inches into the formula, we get:\n\\[\nV = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi (3)^3\n\\]\n\nNow calculate \\( 3^3 \\):\n\\[\n3^3 = 27\n\\]\n\nSubstitute back into the formula:\n\\[\nV = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\times 27\n\\]\n\nSimplify the expression:\n\\[\nV = \\frac{4 \\times 27}{3} \\pi = \\frac{108}{3} \\pi = 36 \\pi\n\\]\n\nThus, the volume of the inscribed sphere is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{36 \\pi \\text{ cubic inches}}\n\\]",
